2026-10-08  Test A: DMbot writes down what one person says (owner, alone): FAIL
==============================================================================
  - 05:43-05:45 UTC on fba4f77, Deepgram, from docs/next-test-step.md. The owner was on
    a phone (5G). Steps 1-7 done: /dmbot start (campaign "Test subject"), session
    started, the sentence said once, waited ~15 s, /dmbot stop.
  - Result: the transcript channel shows "Session started" and "Session ended" with no
    line between. Start, consent and stop worked.
  - Server: ears "capturing user" at 05:44:17.825, then 160 ms later "receive error ...
    Failed to decrypt: DecryptionFailed(UnencryptedWhenPassthroughDisabled)"; health
    received=1 expected=1. core: "Capture check: 1 x speech, 0.0 s, audio 100%",
    "Listened 2.0 min, sent 0.0 min of speech (0%)". Nothing reached Deepgram.
  - Cause so far: the DM's client sent audio that wasn't end-to-end encrypted while the
    bot's DAVE session expected it; after 36 failed packets the voice library ends the
    subscription and ears waits for the next pause to subscribe again. The audio %
    didn't show the loss. Bug #631. First such error in 30 h of ears logs.
  - Next: Test A again to see if it repeats; ears to log the DAVE handshake (#631).

